econd figure is the longest run the surviving fixes show, not proof that the continuous hold was broken — the gap leaves that open, so the limb is undecided and supports neither a payment nor a refund. The $4.00 figure itself is correct (cancellation_fee 4.00, base_fare 0.00, platform_fee 0.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and the 4.00 equals the GREATER of the STANDARD zone-class fee and the RYDE_X tier fee, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect) — but no refund issues, because the case escalates.\n\nWhy escalation, and at what confidence. POL-NS-08 provides that where the ONLY evidence for the deciding fact is impaired under its limbs (a) to (d), the ruling may not exceed PARTIAL_REFUND and the case escalates under POL-NS-09; the deciding fact here is the effective continuous in-geofence dwell, it is carried solely by EV-GPS-00211, and that artifact is impaired under limb (b). POL-NS-09(e) is therefore engaged, and POL-NS-09(a) is engaged too: the confidence cap is the minimum weight_multiplier among the artifacts carrying the deciding fact — 0.39 — and no independent artifact carries that same fact, so the cap is not lifted to a maximum. 0.39 is below the policy confidence_floor of 0.70 (POL-NS-09(a)). Confidence is stated as 0.39. The driver's anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 2, and 2/146 = 1.4%, below both thresholds), so no POL-NS-07 instruction enters the packet, and no false-arrival referral arises because qualifying in-geofence fixes do exist.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer. The reviewer must settle whether the driver in fact held position inside the pickup geofence continuously across 12:33:40–12:36:28 — that is, whether the effective continuous dwell reached the 300-second minimum. The trace's missing 168 seconds is the single fact that decides whether the fee stands (with SGD 3.20 driver compensation) or is refunded in full, and it should be resolved from the underlying device telemetry or any advisory record 